  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 352 PM CDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nFocus in the long term turns to a more active weather \npattern setting up heading into the weekend and early next week. \nDiscrepancies still remain between the models with the \ndisturbance late Friday into Saturday, leading to lower \nconfidence in the track of the system and duration, as one \nsolutions leads to more widespread coverage of precipitation, \nand another solution pushes the system a little further east, \nfavoring less precipitation chances across western Nebraska. \nAlthough there is lower confidence in the placement of the \nprecipitation, there is at this time better confidence in the \ntemperatures remaining above freezing so do expect precipitation\nmode to mainly be all rain Friday into Saturday. \n\nTowards the end of the forecast period, a stronger, more organized \nsystem, potentially a closed low system tracks in off the Pacific \nCoast over the weekend and slowly ejects into the Central Plains by \nearly next week. High uncertainty still exist with this system as it \nremains off the coast and there will still be the potential for \nchanges with the track of the system as it continues to evolve, but \nsomething worth watching over the upcoming forecast.",
